rsed from the point $P(1,2)$ to point $Q(4,4),$ then ${\\int }_{C}(x-y)\\,dx+(x+y)\\,dy=$" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383196 1113 #uuid "5ccef1ed-ef2f-5e8d-8fa8-49b0d783b043" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383196 1145 "Notice that our curve is given by the explicit Cartesian equation $y=2\\sqrt{x}.$ As a result, we obtain the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j={t}^{2}\\,i+2t\\,j,\\,t\\in [1,2]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=2t\\,i+2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(x-y)\\,dx+(x+y)\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(x-y)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+(x+y)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}((x-y)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+(x+y)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}({t}^{2}-2t)\\cdot 2t+({t}^{2}+2t)\\cdot 2\\,dt \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{2}t({t}^{2}-2t)+({t}^{2}+2t)\\,dt \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}+2t\\,dt \\\\  & =2{[\\frac{{t}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+{t}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2[(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}+{2}^{2})-(\\frac{{1}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3}+{1}^{2})] \\\\  & =2[4-\\frac{8}{3}+4-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{3}-1] \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{53}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{53}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383197 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383198 13194139536091 true] [17592186383197 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383199 13194139536091 true] [17592186383197 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383200 13194139536091 true] [17592186383197 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383201 13194139536091 true] [17592186383197 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383202 13194139536091 true] [17592186383197 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536091 true] [17592186383197 1041 "selection" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383197 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383202 13194139536091 true] [17592186383197 1110 #uuid "fe52b476-1e76-5c31-8c42-ec2e48a10f12" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383198 1034 "\\frac{42}{7}" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383198 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536091 true] [17592186383198 1111 #uuid "99d08db5-5831-57fa-96bd-2b2e94d86303" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383199 1034 "\\frac{49}{8}" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383199 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536091 true] [17592186383199 1111 #uuid "ca978376-1d2c-5c47-bf28-b7fb6d7950b9" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383200 1034 "8" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383200 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536091 true] [17592186383200 1111 #uuid "f0e8d3c0-5933-59b6-967e-7d4583c36ca1" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383201 1034 "6" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383201 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536091 true] [17592186383201 1111 #uuid "fa2163b8-59b2-515a-9994-d4d556d9ac34" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383202 1034 "\\frac{53}{6}" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383202 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536091 true] [17592186383202 1111 #uuid "915db1bb-ea43-51c3-9beb-d012be218d29" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383203 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383204 13194139536091 true] [17592186383203 1089 "q-124665" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383203 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536091 true] [17592186383203 1100 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}dx+\\frac{2}{x}\\,dy,$ where $C$ is part of the ellipse $9{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9$ traversed in the counterclockwise direction from the point $(-1,0)$ to the point $(0,-3).$" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383203 1113 #uuid "47948794-c19d-5fb2-9c5b-1aef41a0ecff" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383203 1145 "Since $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $1$ and $3,$ respectively, it can be parametrized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,t\\in [\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}dx+\\frac{2}{x}\\,dy & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{2}{x}\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}(\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2}{x}\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+6\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+6t]_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+9\\pi )-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +6\\pi ) \\\\  & =(0+9\\pi )-(-1+6\\pi ) \\\\  & =3\\pi +1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383205 13194139536091 true] [17592186383204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383206 13194139536091 true] [17592186383204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383207 13194139536091 true] [17592186383204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383208 13194139536091 true] [17592186383204 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383209 13194139536091 true] [17592186383204 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536091 true] [17592186383204 1041 "selection" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383204 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383205 13194139536091 true] [17592186383204 1110 #uuid "6e081e77-5eac-54c3-96d1-b40683f8ba62" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383205 1034 "3\\pi +1" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383205 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536091 true] [17592186383205 1111 #uuid "13e6d829-2a88-5644-891b-5e3578fc97cd" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383206 1034 "4\\pi " 13194139536091 true] [17592186383206 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536091 true] [17592186383206 1111 #uuid "36257285-c3de-51d8-bbc5-b02549c0390a" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383207 1034 "\\frac{3\\pi +1}{2}" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383207 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536091 true] [17592186383207 1111 #uuid "ab6a4d83-1dd1-5c5e-8e5a-8efa553af1c8" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383208 1034 "3\\pi -4" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383208 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536091 true] [17592186383208 1111 #uuid "4545096a-fe21-5515-9523-3a9dced7d27e" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383209 1034 "2\\pi -1" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383209 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536091 true] [17592186383209 1111 #uuid "aa620ab4-ea7d-5a55-a1b6-e5d549c914c3" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383210 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383211 13194139536091 true] [17592186383210 1089 "q-81102" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383210 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536091 true] [17592186383210 1100 "If the path $C$ is the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from the point $A(0,1)$ to the point $B(2,3),$ then ${\\int }_{C}{e}^{x}\\,dx-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi y}{2})\\,dy=$" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383210 1113 #uuid "11e0340d-a912-56e9-bdaf-8b1fda948873" 13194139536091 true] [17592186383210 1145 "The position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=j$ and $b=2\\,i+3\\,j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =j+t(2\\,i+3\\,j-j) \\\\  & =j+t(2\\,i+2j) \\\\  & =2t\\,i+(1+2t)\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x(t)=2t$ and $y(t)=1+2t$ along the segment.\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=2\\,i+2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{e}^{x}\\,dx-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi y}{2})\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi y}{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x